# Triaged findings of tests/hardening/static-analysis, without line numbers.
# Each finding is followed by the reason it is accepted. Generated with
# GCC 15, Clang 21, cppcheck 2.19, flawfinder 2.0.19 and shellcheck 0.11 on
# armv7, aarch64 and x86-64 against Qt 5.15; other tool and Qt versions
# may report more or less.

clang-tidy: plugins/declarative/src/voicecallaudiorecorder.cpp: returning a constant reference parameter may cause use-after-free when the parameter is constructed from a temporary [bugprone-return-const-ref-from-parameter]
  why: QDBusArgument operator>> must return the const QDBusArgument & it was given; Qt's D-Bus marshalling signature
clang-tidy: plugins/declarative/src/voicecallhandler.cpp: an assignment within an 'if' condition is bug-prone [bugprone-assignment-in-if-condition]
  why: intentional: 'if (!(d->connected = success))' style, assignment is the point and is parenthesised
clang-tidy: plugins/declarative/src/voicecallmanager.cpp: an assignment within an 'if' condition is bug-prone [bugprone-assignment-in-if-condition]
  why: intentional: 'if (!(d->connected = success))' style, assignment is the point and is parenthesised
clang-tidy: plugins/filter/lib/filter.cpp: repeated branch body in conditional chain [bugprone-branch-clone]
  why: filter rules are applied in priority order (exact match before pattern match); same action from different rules is the point
clang-tidy: plugins/providers/telepathy/src/callchannelhandler.cpp: Call to virtual method 'CallChannelHandler::startedAt' during construction bypasses virtual dispatch [clang-analyzer-optin.cplusplus.VirtualCall]
  why: the handler classes are not subclassed; the call is meant to reach this class's own implementation
clang-tidy: plugins/providers/telepathy/src/callchannelhandler.cpp: switch has 2 consecutive identical branches [bugprone-branch-clone]
  why: one case per Tp::CallState kept on purpose, so each telepathy state's mapping is explicit
clang-tidy: plugins/providers/telepathy/src/farstreamchannel.cpp: an assignment within an 'if' condition is bug-prone [bugprone-assignment-in-if-condition]
  why: intentional: 'if (!(d->connected = success))' style, assignment is the point and is parenthesised
clang-tidy: plugins/providers/telepathy/src/farstreamchannel.cpp: do not cast 'FsConference *' (aka '_FsConference *') to 'GstElement *' (aka '_GstElement *') through 'void *'; use reinterpret_cast instead [bugprone-casting-through-void]
  why: GLib/GStreamer instance cast macros (GST_ELEMENT, G_OBJECT, ...) cast through gpointer by design; checked casts at runtime with G_TYPE_CHECK_INSTANCE_CAST
